  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; governmental funds only (School Nutrition and Activities are inside Other Governmental Funds); business_type null. Basic receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds statement Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5). Total column nets the 50,000 interfund transfers (General out, Other funds in) to zero, so transfers_in/out are null; debt proceeds 7,929,416 (Special Building bond proceeds) are listed under other financing sources and are outside printed total receipts. Identity: 3,203,330 + 7,215,735 - 6,680,341 + 7,929,416 = 11,668,140. Detail: General Fund detail combines the General Fund budget schedule receipts (pp9-10, more detailed) with Depreciation and Employee Benefit interest (their transfer-in of 500,000 is eliminated by the reclassification column on p7) so revenue ties to the combining Total 5,973,318; General Fund disbursements use the combining schedule Total column (p8, after reclassifications, includes the 50,000 transfer) rather than the budget schedule's pre-reclassification lines, which contain a hidden 500,000 transfer to Depreciation; the General Fund budget disbursement schedule (p11) is therefore not repeated to avoid double counting. The combining page's Depreciation Fund 'Capital outlay' 202,124 is recorded from the more detailed Depreciation Fund schedule (p12): Capital outlay 57,924 + Vehicle acquisition 144,200. Other receiving-fund transfers: School Nutrition +20,000 and Activities +30,000 equal the General Fund's 50,000. Printed zero/blank 2025 lines (e.g. 1980 refund, 4518 IDEA with budget only) omitted. Balance sheet (user 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets, liabilities and fund balances (p6), Total Governmental Funds column. Attempt 2 (audit findings 2026-10-28): Community service operation -> Community Service Operations (statement and detail); 2110 County fines and license fees -> Fines and Licenses; statement 'County receipts' 24,271 split per p9 into Fines and Licenses 24,096 and ESU Receipts 175; Depreciation Fund capital outlay replaced by its p12 object lines. Attempt 3 (verifier fixes 2026-10-28): School Nutrition 'Other receipts' 1,046 (p14) and QCPU 'Other receipts' 326 (p17) -> other / Other / Miscellaneous Receipts per category_decisions.csv; statement 'Other local receipts' 5,291 -> Rentals (dominant 4,965 rental of school equipment, review); detail[0] schedule name corrected to the p9 budget schedule; Depreciation/Employee Benefit interest labels restored as printed (fund in department). Read pages 1-18 of 18"
